      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3175704361",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "For one thing, we propose a self-classification enhancement module that integrates intra-class binary classification (ICBC) to bridge the gap between the two distinct MCC tasks.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:268c5e2882cad121e6ae5dfcacce5c2052a2ccaa734414d714f3535329e40e93",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "69bf82c3a0df4a4d28d540e198a7226503bf789d8c7443d0549746c774605a42",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:31:02.052810Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:14f87b1d701f67df72908ac9dc4bc6201f1cff352b9327b0aad11398dd3f534e#results[12];abstract[554:731]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414360156",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Most previous best-performing methods adopt affinity learning or metric learning.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:2b25a0c5fc8d3b1d88f8df63929a0293e68d86906218c502f78df33888935761",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d70da3a715b527643a78154b1317369548340dfb93e7eb20ae919228c48495e8",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:20.910201Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:50f87666a6fd89ecd3474ba7a6e8fa5756db63b767926645e12e8688613218f7#results[21];abstract[232:313]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385767927",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Our method defines specific transform functions to simulates the local structure change of intra-class in the initial image domain, and formulates a self-supervised learning procedure to fully exploit this property and preserve it in the embedding space.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:2d20a8bfc5df5d39c5660036045cd9edd22977ff641b445c1d7f1b4c48d95d59",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "06241ec0021021ca0cf4d8dd96d1e4df1e3a2cf8c7a980f4ce3af591b9c26db3",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:25.535775Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:e3d0c3a9ccad0b51d4f6af83f7ba490de2bf0d5d521dd712434b62cd06fd9c8c#results[33];abstract[910:1164]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3175505770",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Therefore, we propose a Part Agent Learning Network (PALN) to leverage part features from two aspects.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:2eecbeebc4c271a593d00f5f71f904ced9cdcf0f213d2c67548761c4fe980325",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "8815c7e041f21abc403df63f04cff330229e46e7cd4f509b5b0aea8b1ad1aba2",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:40.732787Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:d28f921c2cca0500fefbd59cc788a272466f0e1d839cba716932ee769a56d2fc#results[49];abstract[487:589]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409367300",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "While previous approaches relied on extensive image-text pairs or dense semantic annotations, recent training-free methods attempted to overcome these limitations by constructing semantic prototypes in the construction stage and image-to-image matching (i.e., prototype matching) during testing.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:30028427c951bb0e0127542822f6ba142b031129c9484ff829c9fed75d979220",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "52e1ad134f6ceca73396c261d26cb7d3ca6cf596ae5d67c1c4676c97513f64a5",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:56.080577Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:40aa6b86fb4e80d0619dc24f5f79dd9b5449cf9c0203b77c8af8d92d66bc3da6#results[49];abstract[119:414]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409366327",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Moreover, to mitigate the impact of noise in user-bundle interaction data, we propose to map the bundle representations into a set of learnable prototypes, and we further propose a prototype learning module to combine the composition patterns with interaction signals for tail bundles.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:3c75ca392a86ea83d49e3aba0baccba5cbfcab250284774eac24463a6c3c942c",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "ae1e14d9bf297eb2f69ad86bc9328b5f9ed5e9c2c6fcd266680ff58913110df3",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:31:06.039389Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:dd2669bbe78b8fdbaf5b6b50d06b6856ca83d1a57b22d25dd62d930a822f125a#results[23];abstract[1240:1525]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414360168",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Our approach initiates with pre-training a diagnosis model with dual regularizers, which decouples student states into domain-shared and domain-specific parts.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:43414d1d61cc84be5f8808aa1916e7edf8e7a80d29d63425cabd56fbcee30e52",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "574f7c6f22b1a74f85c04bdb4f1b32990d660a6d60dab931164657b227c49ef4",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:41.106011Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:5b4bb370e08627374de6bf0cfc9353e0fca71fb23b2c02683f54ce6c960e021b#results[12];abstract[935:1094]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393148098",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To this end, we propose a novel PEFT learning approach tailored for dense prediction tasks, namely VFM-Adapter.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:434955076e08103e8ac33bfb6d4e6793ef9cca98886b47db72b8fbe944278dab",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d4af3206ef5d7cc89af9f98070056a6b791f622e7b0e573190c433f23769e860",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:29.288830Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:c1c9262e50eb3cad37d82e4e43fd5cb7ec21721cc9a62eb930c22b035aa15b69#results[40];abstract[646:757]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409369930",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "After training, Our network is concatenated with simple task-specific back-ends and fine-tuned for different shape analysis tasks.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:43c5ba36a1a16b8a87964754a6ace6e7b23b7199fe85d4f0e309f79fbc80f424",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "087c4fc82972d3feda637e8c9be27fdd789056436f29422eaf777037084e5099",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:31.254032Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:691f737e4a266368137cb11d51e38dfaeeeb671d8de87f6c7b508dea8f20c553#results[19];abstract[617:747]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3173636389",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Drawing inspiration from the analogy between latent channels and frequency components, we examine domain gaps in LIC and observe that out-of-training-domain images disrupt pre-trained channel-wise decomposition.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:4fadf9d63af40666f69830bba8b46cf61bac6d9e767802ee113d9d386f01c5e2",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "52e1ad134f6ceca73396c261d26cb7d3ca6cf596ae5d67c1c4676c97513f64a5",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:56.080577Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:40aa6b86fb4e80d0619dc24f5f79dd9b5449cf9c0203b77c8af8d92d66bc3da6#results[29];abstract[484:695]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409365119",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Specifically, we map the transformed input images with different views and appearances into the same embedding space, and then mutually estimate the pairwise relationships of embeddings generated from the original input and its transformed variants.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:500314a44fffcce97c71110c4f5256dda45133a8ee464b9967c5a885a3033bf2",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "8c684456737c55e56ef3af175dc422f8fa292155972e1e652a3522022648bc47",
