      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3175918389",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To address such a challenge, many methods exploit a base set consisting of massive labeled samples to learn an instance embedding function, i.e., image feature extractor, and it is expected to possess good transferability among different tasks.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:81b91410ec4c8712142365cba44c2ddf7ecb7fb2477c5497c99beff3876b682b",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "24b6e032ea3fde9a71dbf3042c0600e1b44a42e91a404001b40bf44afeb4a65c",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:57.803701Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:b18fd6478584a9b842cda2072101848fc23a2188e31ed1eaef6e5f3c06f90ac8#results[9];abstract[106:350]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3176219570",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Specifically, we propose self-augmented editability learning to enhance the editability for projected embedding, which is achieved by constructing paired generated celebrity's face and edited celebrity images for training, aiming at transferring mature editability of off-the-shelf text-to-image models in celebrity to unseen identities.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:84ac75fe446b1b3fabb62a33d05fc96b5cc98cc4103cc7bfc6cf1212c14fa552",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "1ea4c7b596c3f806cfda7568b5b431d7f136adad03c0b2d51dca4e52a88c434d",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:17.441610Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:972cae2fd4e55a276fbc3f57a411870fef27928905fa48c330bc9ad5092d33b0#results[17];abstract[570:907]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393149651",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Worse still, current invariant representation learning methods in recommendation neglect even hurt the representation discriminability due to data sparsity and label shift.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:871ce5704117b92a03e10d1caeb39984e6d4d227bfffa6cd328f1feb66303687",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "7a2e64ae41a687242a99fc98b29089a552aa73e206bf44b0e7c5d3a1ba19ae92",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:23.328057Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:8fbadd4d5611e2cde37692d567262013f0af08c2a4767f5d96cfa2bada53bf69#results[20];abstract[484:656]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385767887",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Particularly, as the generated images may have different distributions from the original data, TIKP transfers the knowledge by a content adaption loss, which determines the role played by the generated images in incremental training based on the similarity.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:8a103d20be1ac7cdd6337ece9aa6e5e3402a273f6bc3986547efef3b2c1cf94c",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "8fce3befc6f4083d7aeb37b278d795b1cd5a1b218818613e4a90de36f23959c8",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:08.298788Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:4fcdf484d6ee314bb4d8f022396f823e8116701df50393f466829bf3ad35d7c4#results[30];abstract[611:868]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393160060",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Specifically, we first utilize the dynamic information from the event signal as prior knowledge, and integrate it into existing de-raining objectives to better constrain the solution space.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:8b9f694aa38785e658f895c2100b41648ec211e20c05b4b3f99a4da77ca5e693",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "20f6a8e3b06a5212d7b2fa6e56ec955c233aa6d4dc561829a888f9e26e2b7cba",
