      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393158951",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To be specific, we design a neural network-based data augmentation module with priori bias to find out what meets the teacher's strengths but the student's weaknesses, by learning magnitudes and probabilities to generate suitable data samples.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:8f6ddd5b5e1e1e110cc9b5b0c35fd37f5a493d700d924e2bb8f2687356d3d541",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d70da3a715b527643a78154b1317369548340dfb93e7eb20ae919228c48495e8",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:20.910201Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:50f87666a6fd89ecd3474ba7a6e8fa5756db63b767926645e12e8688613218f7#results[44];abstract[514:757]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385768260",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To solve these issues, this paper proposes attentive feature regularization (AFR) which aims to improve the feature representativeness and discriminability.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:934783c4e995448aa88463baa8de9ce751078b6000e69100add0ddb79bd0bdf3",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "27af0c8d41d90e604d6510007a95d47eff078224ef794752414b0afbd14ba48e",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:39.464871Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:a66d7023458ae7290b95f381f6993e33c7325dafab57636ddc620ef5c38890e0#results[11];abstract[375:531]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393147864",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "In this study, we argue an ideal subject representation can be achieved by a cross-differential perspective, i.e., decoupling subject intrinsic attributes from irrelevant attributes via contrastive learning, which allows the model to focus more on intrinsic attributes through intra-consistency (features of the same subject are spatially closer) and inter-distinctiveness (features of different subjects have distinguished differences).",
      "id": "evidence:topic:9445c399314a143788e8dd33551ef10e03f2f49ab183627010abcf1ce70d321a",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d4af3206ef5d7cc89af9f98070056a6b791f622e7b0e573190c433f23769e860",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:29.288830Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:c1c9262e50eb3cad37d82e4e43fd5cb7ec21721cc9a62eb930c22b035aa15b69#results[12];abstract[702:1139]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409346376",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Our GL-RG demonstrates three advantages over the prior efforts: 1) we explicitly exploit extensive visual representations from different video ranges to improve linguistic expression; 2) we devise a novel global-local encoder to produce rich semantic vocabulary to obtain a descriptive granularity of video contents across frames; 3) we develop an incremental training strategy which organizes model learning in an incremental fashion to incur an optimal captioning behavior.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:9621a38ad04fb667b8ddfe23facab6c05a7a451b8303e784690950244c9bc378",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "6252091c118b9bb68660c27d8e6f0032eebead3e1cf6b1f74696c9dc4e005ea1",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:10.030956Z",
